WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
[Vaati:] Hey, what's up guys? I'm Vaati.
[HellkiteDrake:] and I'm HellkiteDrake.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:08.040
[Vaati:] And today, we are going to show you five things you *definitely* didn't know about Dark Souls.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:12.340
So usually with this series, I say that if you learn something new then you should leave a like,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.960
but honestly, you guys aren't gonna get any of these. Hellkite is amazing at digging around in the game's files,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.260
So these are things the average person just wouldn't know.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:26.400
Now it's not that I'm doubting you; it's just, don't get too upset if you don't get many, ok? You'll see what I mean.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.080
If you still want to play the game with the like system then how about: If you learn 5 new things then you leave a like,

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.120
and if you know *anything* on the list then feel free to leave a dislike, guilt free.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.960
Anyway, all five of these things are awesome. So let's get started, but what should we start off with, man?

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.960
[Hellkite Drake:] I think we should start off with undead King Jarr-Eel.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.040
Number one: There's a cut or scrapped boss named Undead King Jarr-Eel.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:56.240
Undead King Jarr-Eel seems to be a boss who was cut from development. His name indicates that he is either a king of the Undead or a King who is undead.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.320
I believe it's more likely that he was a King over New Londo, which according to the Crestfallen Warrior,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.080
[Crestfallen Warrior voice clip:] "It was once an Undead City."

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:10.240
The cut dialogue from Ingward Indicates Jarr-Eel may have been fought atop the church roof where Ingward ended up standing.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.600
He's referred to as a Darkwraith which we know to be true since he fights with a Dark Hand, a tool of the Darkwraiths.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.560
It's likely that he was the one that Ingward was referring to.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.520
Jarr-Eel wields a Dark Hand that he can use as his shield, punch, and maybe even drain humanity with.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.480
There's actually a level draining effect still left in the game that will flash with red text,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.680
similar to the text that appears when equipment breaks or when you're cursed.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:35.120
He also has the same sound bites as King Allant from Demon's Souls who was able to drain soul levels.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.120
Not to mention, Jarr-Eel and the Four Kings share the same AI script, indicating that he may have been

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.880
scrapped in favor of the four kings or may have had a script repurposed for the boss fight.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.320
The four Kings seem to wear a corrupted version of his armor with a crescent spike

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.640
coming out from his shoulder and pieces that move outwards from the middle.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.040
The Four Kings were once rulers of humanity, corrupted by the Dark

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.400
and there are many conclusions to be drawn from the similarities between the two.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:02.920
Defeat Undead King Jar-Eel and you'll get the Key to the Seal from Ingward along with his brilliant armor.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.080
[Vaati:] Number two: as you can see Frampt and Kaathe have more animations than are currently in the game.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:16.280
By replacing the model of Frampt or Kaathe over the AI of characters with attack or death animations,

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.160
you can see these terrifying and often hilarious animations.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:26.120
Obviously when they created Frampt and Kaathe, they were meant to be killable enemies, but man, I'm kind of glad you can't kill them.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:32.480
I prefer to think of them as these mysterious immortal beings even though they're already this goofy looking snake with a moustache.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.880
And if this head smash animation was in the game it might have shattered that already fragile image.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.440
And speaking of attack animations...

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:44.560
[Hellkite:] Number three: the living trees in the Darkroot Garden have attack animations.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.680
They can swipe down at you with their vines.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:52.040
This was probably left unused so that the trees could trick players into thinking that the path is blocked by a real tree.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.160
[Vaati:] Number four and five both have to do with Priscilla.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:59.059
Did you know that Priscilla has unique sitting and standing animations?

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:05.480
According to the Dark Souls Designworks interviews, Priscilla was originally going to be a sort of heroine character.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.339
Miyazaki later elaborated saying that her role was replaced by the Fire Keepers.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:17.080
A variety of sitting poses are reminiscent of the Maiden in Black from Demon's Souls who was always sitting in a different way in the Nexus.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.560
Did you also know that every enemy in the Burg was originally meant to be Priscilla?

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.000
I'm just kidding, just kidding...

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.640
And for the final thing - this is your last chance to redeem yourself if you haven't known anything so far.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:35.780
So again, according to the Designworks interviews, the Painted World was originally a prototype map, one of the first the developer worked on.

00:03:36.209 --> 00:03:41.389
Personally, I think this is why it's such a well designed level; there's absolutely no signs that they rushed it.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:49.120
There's a variety of enemies to fight, the level has great pacing, it loops around brilliantly, and there's a lot of different situations you can get yourself into.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.680
Anyway, back on topic: the final thing you didn't know.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:04:00.040
So in Priscilla's boss room, there's actually a 3D mesh for a breaking floor which is similar to the breaking floor where you fight the Stray Demon in the Asylum.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:08.040
Not only this but we know that Nito was originally placed in the game's prototype map, which as I've said before is the Painted World of Ariamis.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:12.840
So we can only assume that Nito was originally placed below this breaking floor.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:17.840
There are even spiraling stairs that lead back up from the fall right below if you look at a map viewer.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:23.000
So this was obviously an earlier version of Nito before he found a more appropriate home in the Catacombs,

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.320
you know, where he could wear a different skeleton for every day of the week.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.920
And that's it! If you were playing a game with the like system, then leave a like if you learned five new things today.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.640
And that's not all! If you're hungry for more cut content,

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:38.880
Then go check out Hellkite Drake's channel. His will be the first link in the description.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.840
He has an entire series devoted to cut content so if you're looking for more, that's the place to be.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:48.840
Not only that but he also makes great remixes of the game soundtrack so go check it out.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:54.160
And if you're looking for more things you didn't know about Dark Souls then click the playlist link on the screen.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.560
Cheers guys, I'll see you in the next one.

